cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
  If you use the FlyWire data, please also cite the FlyWire publications
  listed under references and the others given in data/README.md.
type: software
title: "A spiking neural network wired like the auditory circuit of Drosophila"
abstract: >-
  A spiking neural network, simulated in Brian2, whose wiring is the
  auditory subgraph of Johnston's organ in the FlyWire v783 connectome of
  Drosophila melanogaster (1,239 neurons and 20,059 connections). Trained
  with spike-timing-dependent plasticity (STDP) and winner-take-all
  inhibition, it classifies the inter-pulse interval of synthetic fly
  courtship songs (five classes, from 25 to 65 ms) with an accuracy of
  0.875, against 0.768 for a configuration-model control and 0.443 for an
  Erdős–Rényi control trained with the same rule. Plasticity improves only
  the connectome significantly. The repository follows the phases of
  CRISP-DM and includes the data pipeline, the experiments, their stored
  outputs, a reproduction guide and an interactive web demo.
authors:
  - family-names: "Mora"
    given-names: "Luis"
    affiliation: "Universidad Técnica Particular de Loja"
  - family-names: "Alvarez"
    given-names: "Jean"
    affiliation: "Universidad Técnica Particular de Loja"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ljmor/flywire-snn-stdp"
keywords:
  - spiking neural network
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - Drosophila melanogaster
  - Johnston's organ
  - spike-timing-dependent plasticity
  - Brian2
  - neuromorphic computing
  - CRISP-DM
